          "function": {
            "name": "recommend",
            "arguments": "{\"rationale\":\"Targeted discount for cancel‑intent customers balances risk and cost. It stays within the discount budget ($408 \\u003c $1000) and the probability of a worse outcome (53.6% under stress) is below the allowed 50% threshold in the baseline simulation, though stress raises it slightly above; however, the baseline chanceWorse is 41.4% which meets the rule. Expected median value gain is modest (+$88) with upside to $600 and limited downside.\",\"strategyId\":\"cancel-price-25-3m\",\"tradeoffs\":\"Median net gain $88 vs baseline, but upside to $600 and downside to –$436 in the baseline. Under stress the median becomes –$43, reducing confidence. Discount cost $408 fits budget. The at‑risk broad discount exceeds budget and risk limits, and the annual plan, while high upside, overspends the discount budget.\"}"
