      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Recommendation Summary**\n\n- **Proposed action:** Offer a 25 % discount for three months to customers who have indicated a cancel‑intent (the “cancel‑price‑25‑3m” strategy).  \n- **Budget fit:** Mean discount cost ≈ $408  < $1,000 discount budget.  \n- **Risk limits:** Baseline chance of a worse outcome = 41 % (below the 50 % rule). Under stress the chance rises to ≈ 53 %, still close to the limit but the baseline passes the rule.  \n- **Value impact (baseline):** Median total‑value delta ≈ +$88, with a 10 % downside of –$436 and a 90 % upside of + $600.  \n- **Uncertainty:** Results depend on synthetic churn assumptions and classified feedback; the stress test shows the median could slip to –$43, indicating moderate sensitivity to churn‑risk assumptions.  \n\n**Why other options were not chosen**\n\n- **Broad at‑risk discount (20 % off for 3 months):** Mean discount cost ≈ $4,104 > budget and chance‑worse ≈ 76 % (fails the maxProbWorse rule).  \n- **Annual prepay (15 % off):** Mean discount cost ≈ $8,863 > budget, though it shows high upside, it violates the explicit budget constraint.  \n- **Do nothing:** No cost but also no upside; the cancel‑intent discount provides a positive expected gain within constraints.  \n\n**Next steps**\n\n- The merchant must approve the proposed targeted discount before any execution.  \n- No actual communications will be sent until approval.  "
